REM ============================================================
REM  05 - STRINGS: QUOTES, BACKSLASHES, SPECIAL CHARACTERS
REM  DuckyScript 1.0  ->  Pico Duck OK
REM
REM  STRING types everything after it literally, INCLUDING spaces.
REM  There is no escaping: quote marks are just characters.
REM  The only thing that ends a STRING is the end of the line.
REM ============================================================

DEFAULT_DELAY 40

GUI r
DELAY 700
STRING notepad
ENTER
DELAY 1500

REM Quotes need no escaping - they are typed as-is.
STRING "double quotes" and 'single quotes' both just type.
ENTER

REM Backslashes are literal too - handy for paths.
STRING C:\Users\Public\Documents\report.txt
ENTER

REM Characters that are keystrokes, not text, must be separate lines:
REM   %  is fine inside STRING, but in CMD it can be a variable marker
REM   &  |  <  >  are shell operators - fine in Notepad, dangerous in cmd
REM If you need them in a shell, wrap the whole command in quotes.

REM To type the literal word STRING, just include it in the text:
STRING The word STRING is only a command at the start of a line.
ENTER

REM To type a line that begins with a command word, prepend a space:
STRING  REM this line has a leading space so it is text
ENTER

REM Empty STRING lines are pointless - use ENTER instead.
ENTER

STRINGLN Done. Nothing here executed anything - it is all text.
